---
import config from '../data/contact.json';
---
{config.enabled && <section id="contact-messages"><h2>Messages sent through our contact form</h2><p>We use Formspree to receive contact messages. If you submit the form, your email address, optional name, selected topic, message, and technical request information are processed by Formspree and our email providers so we can receive and answer your enquiry. The submission service may require a Google reCAPTCHA spam check. The form does not subscribe you to a mailing list.</p><p>Contact-message processing is separate from optional Google Analytics. Our own analytics code does not send the contents of contact fields. We do not embed Formspree or reCAPTCHA scripts in this page; submission and any spam check take place through the submission service. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p><p>Messages may be processed outside your country. Please do not include passwords, payment details, or sensitive personal information. You may use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> for a question about a message you previously sent. We process contact messages on the basis of our legitimate interests in answering enquiries, correcting content, and maintaining relevant correspondence. Providing your email address and message is necessary if you want us to receive and answer an enquiry; your name is optional. We keep contact correspondence only for as long as it is needed to handle the enquiry and any related follow-up. We review retained correspondence at least once a year and delete or anonymize messages that are no longer needed, including copies in our email inbox. A completed enquiry alone is not a reason to keep a message indefinitely. Where a continuing business relationship, a legal obligation, or the establishment, exercise, or defense of a legal claim requires particular messages to be retained longer, we keep only the relevant material for as long as that purpose requires. Formspree archive retention is separate from the copies delivered to our inbox; deleting one does not delete the other.</p></section>}
